Hi Jacob,
Unfortunately we aren't sufficiently familiar with Plotly to know how to configure it so that it isn't placing its files outside of the directory that the app runs in. For shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> to work for your applications, the data that it needs has to be contained in the same directory as the application itself.  The application won't have access to ~/XXX, and you will want to access everything as a relative path from where the ui.R and server.R files live.

